# KNOWN GAP, recorded deliberately (see #3264): `step` is VM-INSTRUCTION
# granular, not line granular. Crossing a single source line takes several
# `step over`s, and how many is unpredictable to an author. Every GDB-style
# debugger means "advance one line" by this verb.
#
# This golden records the behaviour as it actually is rather than the
# behaviour we want, so that fixing #3263 shows up here as an intentional
# diff instead of being invisible. Do NOT "fix" this fixture by adding
# steps until the count looks right — that would hide the gap it exists to
# document.
break story.ink:7
run
expect-line 7
step over
step over
step over
step over
expect-line 8
locals
expect-local who = "vendor"
stack
